# SchemaPress
#
# vendor/ and build/ are NOT treated the same way, and the difference is the
# one thing worth understanding here.
#
#   vendor/   ignored — rebuilt by `composer install`, and by `npm run package`
#             with --no-dev on the way into the zip
#   build/    committed — the admin bundles
#
# build/ stays because a change to src/ has to ship compiled, and CI checks the
# committed bundle still matches its source.
#
# vendor/ used to be committed too, on the reasoning that somebody installing
# the plugin has no Composer. That is true of the ZIP, and the zip is built
# with its own --no-dev install, so nothing about distribution needed it in
# git. What it cost was a working tree that was permanently dirty: every
# `composer install` rewrites six tracked files under vendor/composer/, so
# `git add -A` had to be policed, and a whole guard script and CI job existed
# to stop a dev install reaching a release. None of that machinery is needed
# once the directory is simply ignored.
#
# Installing straight from a git clone now needs one extra step:
#
#   composer install

# --- dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/

vendor/

# --- generated at runtime ---------------------------------------------------

# Nothing writes here any more — the Tailwind safelist this described was
# removed, and the plugin now writes no files at all, which is the right answer
# for something installed into a directory it may not own. Kept so a stray
# working copy of the old behavior cannot be committed by accident.
generated/

# --- release artifacts ------------------------------------------------------

# What `npm run package` builds. It is derived from everything else in here and
# is rebuilt in a second; committing one means a repository that grows by a
# megabyte and a half per release for no reason anybody can use.
schemapress.*.zip

# --- local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------

composer.phar
.php-cs-fixer.cache
.phpunit.result.cache
.phpunit.cache/

# --- environment ------------------------------------------------------------

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- editors ----------------------------------------------------------------

.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# --- operating systems ------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- logs and scratch -------------------------------------------------------

*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*~
